# Daily WhatsApp update (trigger: "last prompt")

When the user says **"last prompt"** (or clearly ends a dev session and asks for a daily update), respond with a **WhatsApp-ready message** they can copy-paste and share.

## Output rules

1. **One block only** — plain text, no markdown headers, no code fences.
2. **Short and scannable** — bullets with emoji sparingly (✅ 🔜 ⚠️).
3. **Client-friendly** — outcome-focused, minimal jargon; skip file paths and internal tool names.
4. **Honest status** — separate *Done today*, *In progress*, *Pending / next*, *Blockers* only when relevant.
5. **Include date** at the top (e.g. `Sharnam Portal — Daily update | 21 Sep 2026`).
6. **Do not commit or push** unless explicitly asked in that same message.

## Template

```
Sharnam Portal — Daily update | <date>

✅ Done today
• <outcome 1>
• <outcome 2>

🔜 Next (when we resume)
• <next item 1>
• <next item 2>

⚠️ Blockers (only if any)
• <blocker>
```

Keep to ~5–8 bullets total unless the user asks for detail.

## Scope

Summarize work from the **current conversation/session** (and uncommitted git changes if relevant). If nothing was shipped, say so and list what was explored or drafted.
